 #edb/ref 17592186050810 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522689 #edb/ref 1089 #edb/ref 17592186522691 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522689 #edb/ref 1090 #uuid "18dbf1ce-a447-5af5-bed8-35e9baf14494" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522691 #edb/ref 1084 #edb/ref 17592186522831 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522691 #edb/ref 1084 #edb/ref 17592186522835 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522691 #edb/ref 1084 #edb/ref 17592186522840 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522691 #edb/ref 1084 #edb/ref 17592186522844 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522691 #edb/ref 1084 #edb/ref 17592186522849 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522691 #edb/ref 1084 #edb/ref 17592186522851 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522691 #edb/ref 1084 #edb/ref 17592186522868 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522691 #edb/ref 1084 #edb/ref 17592186522871 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522691 #edb/ref 1084 #edb/ref 17592186522876 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522691 #edb/ref 1084 #edb/ref 17592186522889 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522691 #edb/ref 1085 "Let $f(x)$ be the piecewise function defined below, where $a$ and $b$ are constants. \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+3x, & \\,x\\in (-\\infty ,-4) \\\\ -5a, & \\,x\\in [-4,-2] \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}-1}{x+1} & \\,x\\in (-2,-1)\\cup (-1,\\infty ) \\\\ 2b, & \\,x=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522691 #edb/ref 1086 #uuid "2fbdaa1b-228d-5d0a-abc0-029400c0909b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522691 #edb/ref 1087 #edb/ref 17592186522871 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522695 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186522602 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522695 #edb/ref 1069 "q-133016" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522695 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522695 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the right-sided limit of $f(x)$ at $x=-2.$\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\,-{2}^{+}}f(x)\\,=\\,$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522695 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "03ebca0d-b111-51a4-8281-85b0168f9966" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522695 #edb/ref 1074 "Approaching from the right, we have $-2<x<-1,$ so we use the expression \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}-1}{x+1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,-{2}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,-{2}^{+}}\\frac{{x}^{2}-1}{x+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-2)^{2}-1}{-2+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{-1} \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522699 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186522680 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522699 #edb/ref 1069 "q-133017" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522699 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522699 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to -1}f(x).$ If the limit does not exist, write \"DNE\" (without the quotation marks).\n\n${lim}_{x\\to -1}f(x)\\,=\\,$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522699 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0922b64e-eb7a-5dde-9dd1-94e76b652889" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522699 #edb/ref 1074 "If we attempt to evaluate the limit, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,-1}\\frac{{x}^{2}-1}{x+1}=\\frac{(-1)^{2}-1}{-1+1}=\\frac{0}{0}\n$$\n\nSo, to find the limit, we have to factor the numerator and the denominator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}-1}{x+1} & =\\frac{(x+1)(x-1)}{x+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(x+1)}(x-1)}{\\cancel{x+1}} \\\\  & =x-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,-1}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,-1}\\frac{{x}^{2}-1}{x+1} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,-1}(x-1) \\\\  & =-1-1 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522705 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186522607 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522705 #edb/ref 1069 "q-133022" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522705 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522705 #edb/ref 1071 "Assume once again that $a=-\\frac{4}{5}$ and $b=-1,$ as in the previous part. Find the smallest **integer** value of $h$ such that the extreme value theorem is applicable to $f(x)$ on the interval $[h,3].$\n\n$h\\,=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522705 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1d096d37-4b97-520b-934c-34762c2b679b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522705 #edb/ref 1074 "The extreme value theorem states the following:\n\n> *If $f(x)$ is a continuous function defined on the closed interval $[a,b],$ then $f(x)$ always has at least one global maximum and one global minimum on $[a,b]$*.\n\nSo, the extreme value theorem is only applicable to closed intervals on which the function is continuous.\n\nThe smallest possible integer $h$ such that $f(x)$ is continuous on $[h,3]$ is $h=-1,$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/ab/ab92ed0c59facac4fccb050734aba133474c8a0585c6bd981abe7ea05ed0e6be.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522712 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186522682 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522712 #edb/ref 1069 "q-133023" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522712 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522712 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $f(x)={x}^{2}+3x$ for $x<-4,$ compute the value of ${lim}_{x\\to \\,-5}\\frac{f(x)-f(-5)}{x-(-5)}.$ If the limit does not exist, write \"DNE\" (without the quotation marks).\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\,-5}\\frac{f(x)-f(-5)}{x-(-5)}\\,=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522712 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "33443770-e725-52a7-8dbb-99ea791df2cb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522712 #edb/ref 1074 "First, comparing\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,-5}\\frac{f(x)-f(-5)}{x-(-5)}\n$$\n\nwith the formula for the instantaneous rate of change,\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(a)={lim}_{x\\to \\,a}\\frac{f(x)-f(a)}{x-a},\n$$\n\nwe see that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,-5}\\frac{f(x)-f(-5)}{x-(-5)}={f}^{′}(-5).\n$$\n\nNow, computing the derivative of $f$ for $x<-1,$ we have \n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=2x+3,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(-5)=2(-5)+3=-7.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,-5}\\frac{f(x)-f(-5)}{x-(-5)}=-7.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522734 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186522657 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522734 #edb/ref 1069 "q-133019" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522734 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522734 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x).$ If the limit does not exist, write \"DNE\" (without the quotation marks).\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x)\\,=\\,$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522734 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "68787380-f6be-5299-8d7e-90d33587bc3b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522734 #edb/ref 1074 "First, as $x\\to \\infty ,$ we can assume that $x>-1.$ So, we use the following expression for $f(x):$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}-1}{x+1}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both the numerator and the denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is $x.$ Then, by noting that the reciprocals shrink to $0$ in the limit, we can evaluate the resulting expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{x}^{2}-1}{x+1} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{x}-\\frac{1}{x})}{(\\frac{x}{x}+\\frac{1}{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(x-\\frac{1}{x})}{(1+\\frac{1}{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{x-0}{1+0} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }x \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522761 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186522679 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522761 #edb/ref 1069 "q-133015" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522761 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522761 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that the function $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=-4,$ what is the value of $a?$\n\n$a\\,=\\,$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522761 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9a484d05-16dc-5a62-96c8-679e46043371" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522761 #edb/ref 1074 "At $x=-4,$ the left-sided limit is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,-{4}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,-{4}^{-}}({x}^{2}+3x) \\\\  & =(-4)^{2}+3(-4) \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the right-sided limit is\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,-{4}^{+}}f(x)=-5a.\n$$\n\nIn order for $f(x)$ to be continuous at $x=-4,$ we require that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,-{4}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,-{4}^{+}}f(x) \\\\ 4 & =-5a \\\\ a & =-\\frac{4}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=-4$ for $a=-\\frac{4}{5}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522767 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186522647 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522767 #edb/ref 1069 "q-133018" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522767 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522767 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that the function $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=-1,$ what is the value of $b?$\n\n$b\\,=\\,$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522767 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "af82e941-ed72-5bda-8079-22f3d0e5359a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522767 #edb/ref 1074 "Previously, we found that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,-1}f(x)=-2.\n$$\n\nFor $f(x)$ to be continuous at $x=-1,$ we must have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-1) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,-1}f(x) \\\\ 2b & =-2 \\\\ b & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, for the function to be continuous at $x=-1,$ we need $b=-1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522796 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186522574 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522796 #edb/ref 1069 "q-133014" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522796 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522796 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }f(x).$ If the limit does not exist, write \"DNE\" (without the quotation marks).\n\n${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }f(x)\\,=\\,$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522796 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e3a057d6-ea56-5dc0-9a37-b812d961c933" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522796 #edb/ref 1074 "First, as $x\\to -\\infty ,$ we can assume that $x<-4.$ So, we use the following expression for $f(x):$\n\n$$\nf(x)={x}^{2}+3x\n$$\n\nNow, we identify the leading term and compute its limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }({x}^{2}+3x) & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }({x}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\infty \\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522804 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186522559 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522804 #edb/ref 1069 "q-133021" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522804 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522804 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/8f/8fdadf35d95d884dc3b8445e24525094f830e43190eb3d1a960bbb72eb489b9e.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ for $a=-\\frac{4}{5}$ and $b=-1$ is depicted above.\n\nFrom the graph, the function is continuous but not differentiable at $x\\,=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522804 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f2a0bc3d-d9da-5c57-bc24-c5c37731d915" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522804 #edb/ref 1074 "A function is not differentiable wherever it has a discontinuity, corner, cusp, or vertical tangent.\n\n* At $x=-4$ the function has a corner point, so it's not differentiable there.\n\n* At $x=-2$ the function has a jump discontinuity, so it's not differentiable there.\n\nOf these two points, $f(x)$ is continuous only at $x=-4.$\n\nTherefore, the function $f(x)$ is continuous but not differentiable at $x=-4.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522806 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186522579 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522806 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186522601 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522806 #edb/ref 1069 "q-133020" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522806 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522806 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $a=-\\frac{4}{5}.$ For what values of $k$ does the intermediate value theorem guarantee that $f(x)=k$ has a solution on the interval $x\\in [-5,-4]?$\n\n$k\\,\\in \\,[$\n{{field-1}}\n$,\\,$\n{{field-2}}\n$]$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522806 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f39faa87-98f1-5160-9f77-61fba20bbf35" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522806 #edb/ref 1074 "In part 2, we found that the function $f(x)$ is continuous on $[-5,-4]$ when $a=-\\frac{4}{5}.$ \n\nTherefore, the intermediate value theorem guarantees that $f(x)=k$ has a solution for each value of $k$ between $f(-5)$ and $f(-4).$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-5) & =(-5)^{2}+3(-5) \\\\  & =25-15 \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\nf(-4)=-5\\cdot (-\\frac{4}{5})=4,\n$$\n\nwe must have \n\n$$\nk\\in [4,10].\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522828 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "25ac6782-945e-50dc-8d94-bde045860457" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522828 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186522689 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522831 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186522876 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522831 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "26c63ef3-59a9-517f-a9a3-f135c76d28a6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522831 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186522806 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522835 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186522844 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522835 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3914e941-d414-53f7-bd53-d98c12fd4802" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522835 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186522705 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522840 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186522849 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522840 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "49b44d85-918f-562c-b6da-f7c6722a4acc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522840 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186522699 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522844 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5f50cf59-40f9-5116-a336-b10e4608e318" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522844 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186522712 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522849 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186522851 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522849 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6b6f6769-fd0a-563d-b7ee-ff6c541740f0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522849 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186522767 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522851 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186522831 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522851 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "76bea9a4-8b56-505b-b7d4-a9711e1eacf6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522851 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186522734 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522868 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186522840 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522868 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "afd9c16d-e69b-5748-b12d-5ab58bfb6e79" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522868 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186522695 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522871 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186522889 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522871 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b3a4187b-8722-5579-ab54-d378e87a96e8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522871 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186522796 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522876 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186522835 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522876 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ce3e298f-7e34-5b4b-80b9-d7363682990d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522876 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186522804 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522889 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186522868 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522889 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e2cf5b30-bc2b-5b24-8635-d5b5d78d497c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522889 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186522761 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
